{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T21:58:35.180Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ddb2e572b3dc24915ab9fe76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-03q389","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-03q389","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1748"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1748: drop tinyglobby, fdir and picomatch from the SDK runtime graph so consumers' production audits pass while GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf has no patched picomatch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue 1748 (fleet report): npm audit --omit=dev on a fresh install of @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.11.17 reports 4 high entries (pm-cli via tinyglobby, tinyglobby, fdir, picomatch) for GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf, which marks picomatch through 4.0.7 vulnerable with no patched version. Every extension package that gates releases on a production audit is red without any change of its own, and consumers cannot fix it with overrides because no patched target exists. The only runtime consumer is expandAddGlobEntries in src/sdk/linked-artifacts.ts (pm files/docs/test --add-glob). Remediation: replace tinyglobby with a bounded in-repo directory walk plus an explicit glob matcher that keeps the current semantics (files only, dot files matched, symlinks followed with cycle protection, literal directories never expanded, relative or absolute output by pattern form, sorted and deduplicated) and proves parity against tinyglobby over a fixture tree. The repository-side advisory gate exception is pm-03q389."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["consumer-audit","dependency","gh:1748","picomatch","sdk","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:35.180Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T21:58:35.180Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A fresh install of the packed artifact has no tinyglobby, fdir or picomatch in its production dependency graph and npm audit --omit=dev reports no entry for GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf; --add-glob results are identical to the previous tinyglobby expansion on a parity fixture covering stars, globstars, classes, braces, dot files, symlinks, literal directories, absolute patterns and parent-relative patterns; refusal or bounded behavior for pathological patterns is tested; docs describe the supported glob syntax"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-i7w2"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A clean SDK install passes a production npm audit"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"npm audit --omit=dev reports 4 high entries through tinyglobby, fdir and picomatch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-03q389","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-17T21:58:35.180Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14