{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T22:19:48.525Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ddb2e572b3dc24915ab9fe76","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-gh1748","lineage:pm-gh1748","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-03q389+pm-gh1748","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-gh1748","lineage:pm-gh1748","lineage:pm-i7w2"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.326","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T22:19:48.525Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-17T22:19:48.524Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation: src/core/fs/file-glob.ts replaces tinyglobby in expandAddGlobEntries. Design: one linear pre-pass pairs braces and extglob parentheses (so unclosed constructs never trigger re-parsing), a recursive-descent parser bounded at 32 nesting levels builds an AST, Thompson construction builds an NFA bounded at 50,000 states, and the directory walk advances a lazily built DFA (cache bounded at 10,000 nodes) one code point at a time, pruning any directory whose path can no longer match. No regular expression is involved, so repeated extglobs such as +(*) and star chains stay linear. Parity semantics found by probing tinyglobby 0.2.17 with the previous options (onlyFiles, dot, expandDirectories false, followSymbolicLinks): every bracket expression also matches its literal text (picomatch's default literalBrackets fallback, which is what makes app/[slug]/*.tsx reach a [slug] directory), trailing slashes and a leading ./ are ignored, ../ prefixes are kept, numeric and single-letter brace ranges expand, single-part braces stay literal, POSIX classes work, a run of three stars is a single star, leading ! made tinyglobby return nothing. Deliberate differences, documented in docs/COMMANDS.md: negation is a usage error instead of an empty result; a symlink to a directory already on the walk path is not re-entered (tinyglobby listed a self-loop once); stepped ranges are literal (tinyglobby ignored the step); an escaped leading \\! matches a literal !. tinyglobby moved to devDependencies (repository scripts and the parity test still use it). Side effect found: TypeScript 6 no longer includes @types automatically and the program only received Node types through tinyglobby's declarations, so tsconfig.json now declares types: [node] like the packages and examples configs."}]}],"before_hash":"0c63c9af830778a5c2071394f0af6ac4297e9b743b51447938dacffd9dbebffa","after_hash":"a9a8a1e5b4b05b1443edb2e8abfc8aa856a0c48ad2b05606bdd4d42fccfbacfb","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0fafe2d6540216aa41c68db4629798e5a6e77bf6f022e22fab0feae23033a6d1"}
